{
  "result": "The first thing Mara found in the library\u2019s lost and found was a single red mitten. This was unsurprising. The second thing was a photograph of a kitchen table, taken from underneath. This was more interesting. Someone had written on the back, in blue ink: *This is where I hid.*\n\nShe propped the photograph beside the returns slot. For three days nobody mentioned it. On Thursday, a man in a bicycle helmet stopped, leaned close, and laughed. Mara expected him to claim it, but he only said, \u201cWe had that same ugly linoleum,\u201d and went upstairs to use a computer.\n\nBy Saturday there were two more photographs beside it. One showed the hollow behind a lilac bush. The other showed a laundry basket with a bare foot sticking out. No notes. Mara moved the stack of library card applications to make room. By closing time someone had added a map.\n\nIt was drawn in pencil on the back of a grocery receipt. The aisles were crooked, but Mara recognized the library. An X marked the narrow gap between Biography and the radiator. She went to look. There was nothing there except a warm patch of carpet and a paper clip.\n\nOn Monday she ate her lunch in the gap. From the floor, she could see several old pencils under the shelves and the shoes of people deciding what to read. A child walked past, then backed up. They looked at each other. The child put one finger to his lips.",
